      "observed": "On the FCC Peripherals sheet, the FLASH memory U11 (W25N01GVZEIG_TR) has its VCC pin 8 connected to the +5V power rail.",
      "expected": "The W25N01GVZEIG_TR is a 3.3V NAND flash device; its VCC should be connected to the board's +3.3V rail, not the 5V servo/USB rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: U11 W25N01GVZEIG_TR pin 8 VCC connects to +5V."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "FCC-side FLASH | FCCPeripherals | Winbond W25N01GVZEIG_TR (1 Gb NAND)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3V 2A Regulator (MCUs and Sensors); 5 V feeds the servo/PWM connector bank ... the GPS module, and the CH330 USB-UART bridges."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 3.3V-only NAND flash is exposed to 5V, exceeding its supply rating; it may be damaged or fail to communicate, leaving FCC-side flash storage/logging unavailable.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains a clear power-rail error: the FCC-side W25N01GV NAND flash is powered from +5V instead of +3.3V, which can damage or disable the flash."
}

